Query and operate a versioned Nix workspace interface

Usage: nixspace [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  build       Run the exact Nix-emitted build task roots through the declared runner
  test        Run the exact Nix-emitted test task roots through the declared runner
  benchmark   Time exact Nix-generated commands and enforce their p50/p95 gates
  cache       Inspect declared realized roots against declared public Nix caches
  doctor      Diagnose the host against the exact Nix-generated expectations
  setup       Apply or verify the Nix-generated host expectations
  sync        Clone only missing repositories from an exact Nix-emitted selection
  status      Stream Git status for an exact Nix-emitted selection
  update      Fetch and fast-forward an exact Nix-emitted selection transactionally
  package
  env         Explain one package's exact Nix-selected command environment
  target
  artifact
  resource    Resolve one exact Nix-selected resource path
  executable
  launch
  run         Execute one exact workspace executable through its declared artifact
  graph
  index
  west
  completion  Generate a completion script from the authoritative Clap command tree
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace-root <PATH>   Resolve workspace-relative state and plans from this directory
      --index <PATH>            Read and cache the generated workspace index at this path
      --west-plan <PATH>        Read a versioned Nix-generated West execution plan from this path
      --host-plan <PATH>        Read a versioned Nix-generated host expectation plan from this path
      --nix-config <PATH>       Read or update this Nix configuration file
      --nix-mode <MODE>         Select single-user or daemon Nix configuration behavior [possible values: auto, single-user, daemon]
      --source-plan <PATH>      Read a versioned Nix-generated editable source plan from this path
      --launch-plan <PATH>      Read a versioned Nix-generated launch execution plan from this path
      --resolution-plan <PATH>  Read the versioned Nix-generated local/locked resolution plan from this path
      --benchmark-plan <PATH>   Read a versioned Nix-generated benchmark plan from this path
  -h, --help                    Print help
  -V, --version                 Print version
